    "proseDraft": "It was confirmed that the completed questionnaire goes to Brightwater procurement as a spreadsheet by Friday 2026-10-30, 17:00 CT, with Lena's sections reaching Kwame by Thursday noon. The remaining points were only stated, including questions about the insurance certificate versus coverage amounts, attaching versus referencing the pen test summary, portal versus spreadsheet, and whether Brightwater is set up as EU or US.\n\nConfirmed by participants\n- It was confirmed by Rosa, Kwame and Lena, with a passed recheck, that the completed questionnaire goes to Brightwater procurement as a spreadsheet by Friday 2026-10-30, 17:00 CT, with Lena's sections reaching Kwame by Thursday noon.\n\nStated in the meeting\n- It was stated that Kwame owns the questionnaire back next Friday.\n- It was stated that next Friday is fine and time can be blocked for it.\n- It was stated that the legal and insurance sections will be done and passed to Kwame to merge in.\n- It was stated to put them in the shared folder, not email.\n- It was stated that their procurement lead will be told it is in progress.\n- It was stated that the question will be asked when writing to procurement.\n- It was stated as a question whether insurance wants the certificate itself or just the coverage amounts.\n- It was stated to attach the summary letter, not the full report that needs an NDA.\n- It was stated as a question whether to attach the pen test summary or just reference it.\n- It was stated that a spreadsheet was mentioned because the portal is being replaced.\n- It was stated as a question whether they want it in their portal or as a spreadsheet.\n- It was stated that coverage of security documents will be double-checked.\n- It was stated that both will be answered and flagged.\n- It was stated that it needs to be checked whether Brightwater is set up as EU or US."
